{"id": "EUVD-2026-93395", "enisaUuid": "ade84334-fc13-3833-925b-3bcfab374e45", "description": "tftp-hpa 5.4 before 6.0 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in rewrite_string() in tftpd/remap.c that walks heap memory during jump label searches. Unauthenticated remote attackers can send read or write requests whose filename matches a remap jump rule to crash the forked in.tftpd request handler.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T13:35:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T17:15:34", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/tftp/tftp-hpa.git/commit/?id=6735086fb6475c3e1f1daf9829836b3d06f14291", "https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/tftp/tftp-hpa.git/tree/tftpd/remap.c?h=tftp-hpa-5.4#n762", "https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/tftp/tftp-hpa.git/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tftp-hpa-5.4-before-6.0-out-of-bounds-read-via-tftpd-remap-jump-rule"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-106026", "GHSA-w9pp-27r4-r6rj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "95dabd9f-9ff5-362c-8379-f879db531177", "product": {"name": "tftp-hpa", "vendor": {"name": "H. Peter Anvin"}}, "product_version": "5.4 <6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c2e85604-cbd9-3409-a24a-e099a763307e", "vendor": {"name": "H. Peter Anvin"}}], "isExploited": false}